<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Strumica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Strumica is a town in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>, in the valley of the Strumica river near the borders with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Known in antiquity as Astraion and in Byzantine times as Tiberiopolis, it changed hands repeatedly between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>, Bulgaria and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and was ruled by the Dejanović lords before the Ottoman conquest in the late 14th century.</p></div>
